     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">Dear all,</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">I came across a minor issue using the<span> </span><b>morpho.disparity</b><span> </span>function in the latest version of geomorph.</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\">So taking the example from help file, if one run the following code that include<span> </span><span>covariates (a complex model), then a list is returned with<span> </span><span>extractable </span>objects.</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><br></div><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"></p><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">data(plethodon)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">Y.gpa&lt;-gpagen(plethodon$land, print.progress = FALSE)    #GPA-alignment</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">gdf &lt;- geomorph.data.frame(Y.gpa, species = plethodon$species, </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(189,19,152)\">site = plethodon$site)</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">MD &lt;- morphol.disparity(coords ~ Csize + species*site, groups= ~ species, </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">                        data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">MD$Procrustes.var</span></div><div><br></div><div>But, if we now make the model a bit simpler and exclude covariates, then even though the disparity calculation is performed, the MD object will return as NULL. </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">MD &lt;- morphol.disparity(coords ~ 1, data = gdf, iter = 999, print.progress = FALSE)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">MD</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><span>It is an easy fix though and simply require that an extra function (i.e. &#39;return&#39;) to be added to the script.</span></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><span>... </span></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">if (is.null(groups)) {</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><b>   <span> </span></b>pv.obs &lt;- pv</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">   <span> </span><b>return(</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px;color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><b>pv.obs</b></span><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><b>)</b></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\">    cat(&quot;No factor in formula or model terms from which to define groups.\\n&quot;)</span></div><br></span></span></div><div>all the best,</div><div>Mohamad</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><br><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"></p></div><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><br style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size